part.text:
I have updated `app/page.tsx` to implement the blog posts page using Next.js's modern caching strategy.

I used `unstable_cache` to wrap the `getPosts` function call, configuring it with:
- A cache key of `['posts']`
- A tag of `'posts'` for on-demand revalidation
- A `revalidate` time of 3600 seconds (1 hour)

The build verification confirmed that the route is now set to revalidate every 1 hour.

```tsx
import { getPosts } from '../lib/api';
import { unstable_cache } from 'next/cache';

const getCachedPosts = unstable_cache(
  async () => getPosts(),
  ['posts'],
  { tags: ['posts'], revalidate: 3600 }
);

export default async function Home() {
  const posts = await getCachedPosts();

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Blog Posts</h1>
      <ul>
        {posts.map((post) => (
          <li key={post.id}>
            <h2>{post.title}</h2>
            <p>By {post.author}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </main>
  );
}
```
